  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Blaxel Sandbox for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "Version 0.1.4 moves a DeepSeek Harness Web conversation and its current Git worktree to an independent DSH host in a private Blaxel sandbox. Once the cloud page is ready, model requests and tools continue there with the originating computer offline. Earlier tools-only versions require the original host to stay running.\n\nUse [GUIDE.md](GUIDE.md) for setup and recovery, and [the cloud handoff contract](docs/cloud-session-handoff.md) for implementation status and tested boundaries."
    },
    {
      "section": "Move, continue, review, return",
      "text": "1. Select **Move to Blaxel** in an existing Git-backed conversation. A running task checkpoints after its current tool finishes.\n2. The plugin restores the project, native conversation history, referenced images, and supported child-session history in a private cloud host, then opens the same conversation there.\n3. Continue in the cloud page. **Copy private link** provides access from another device; opening from the original computer renews an expired link automatically.\n4. On the original computer with DSH running, select **Move back to local**. Review changed files and the exact patch, then apply the transfer.\n5. The conversation and checked changes return together. The laptop's original permission policy is restored before it resumes. Move to Blaxel again to include newer local work."
    },
    {
      "section": "Move, continue, review, return",
      "text": "The local copy remains read-only while the cloud owns execution. Compatible local file edits survive the return; conflicts retain both copies and save a recovery patch. Reopening connects to the existing sandbox without uploading a new local snapshot."
    },
    {
      "section": "Session architecture",
      "text": "```text\nLocal DSH -> private Blaxel DSH host -> reviewed files and conversation back locally\n```\n\nBlaxel credentials remain on the original computer. The selected model's portable API key is supplied to the dedicated cloud process so its agent can run independently. Local-only model endpoints and OAuth grants cannot be handed off by this implementation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "DeepSeek Harness is in developer preview and its plugin contracts change between release candidates. Each plugin release pins one DSH version and is verified against it with the full check, a clean-profile install, and a DSH Web boot.\n\n| Plugin | DSH host | Node.js |\n| -- | -- | -- |\n| `0.1.4`, `0.1.3` | `0.1.2-rc.1` | 22.19+, 24+ |\n| `0.1.2`, `0.1.1` | `0.1.2-rc.1` | 22, 24 |\n| `0.1.0` | `0.1.1-rc.2` | 22, 24 |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "When DSH publishes a new version, the plugin is re-verified against it and, when a Host contract moved, a new plugin release pins the new version. Older hosts keep the last plugin release that pinned them."
    },
    {
      "section": "Profile installation",
      "text": "Install the current plugin into the DSH Web profile with the native helpers it requires:\n\n```sh\nnpx --yes --package @blaxel/dsh-sandbox@latest dsh-blaxel plugin --profile web add \\\n  --allow-build=@deepseek-ai/dsh-subprocess-local \\\n  --allow-build=koffi \\\n  --allow-build=node-pty \\"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development installation",
      "text": "```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/blaxel-ai/deepseek-harness-blaxel-sandbox.git\ncd deepseek-harness-blaxel-sandbox\npnpm install\npnpm build"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development installation",
      "text": "`dsh-blaxel` prepares an isolated, pinned DSH 0.1.2-rc.1 runtime on first launch and reuses it afterward. It includes the native history-import extension needed to preserve original timestamps. It uses your existing DSH profile; it does not modify your global DSH installation. Node.js, npm and Git must be available. Keep the same `DSH_HOME` if you use a custom profile.\n\nSign in from **Settings > Blaxel**, or authenticate on the host with `bl login YOUR-WORKSPACE`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development installation",
      "text": "`pnpm check` runs lint, types, unit tests, build, and publint. `pnpm e2e` additionally boots the pinned `dsh-blaxel` runtime with the selected profile and runs the Playwright browser smoke suite (`pnpm exec playwright install chromium` once)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Workspace launch",
      "text": "The launch action is available when the session directory is inside a Git worktree. It:\n\n1. Lists tracked files and unignored untracked files.\n2. Excludes common credential and private-key paths.\n3. Creates a bounded archive without `.git` or `.dsh-blaxel` state.\n4. Restores the worktree under `/workspace` in a Blaxel sandbox.\n5. Restores the same native session ID in a dedicated cloud DSH process.\n6. Opens its authenticated private preview after the cloud host is ready."
    },
    {
      "section": "Workspace launch",
      "text": "The launch panel reports real file counts and the active phase. A failed launch stays in the current session with its error instead of creating an empty page."
    },
    {
      "section": "Workspace launch",
      "text": "Before any sandbox is created, the plugin verifies that the session's selected model route is active and that its resolved credential is configured. If a writable credential is missing, the composer shows a secure provider-specific setup card. Saving the key writes it to the DSH host credential store, verifies the model again, and continues the original sandbox action. The selected portable model API key is forwarded to the cloud process; it is never returned to the browser. Blaxel credentials remain local."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
